WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.600
<b>Saitama Matsugishi Public Elementary</b>

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:28.850
Usuyama-san, are you sure you took 
time off from playing badminton?

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.690
My stamina is still lagging way behind.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:33.260
I've got a long way to go.

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:35.440
Gather up.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.680
I've got something to tell you boys today.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.260
It's about the future of the badminton team.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.510
Ko-san, do you need the bathroom?

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:46.680
Wait until after this.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:47.730
It's not that!

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.400
Toya! Sota!

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:50.750
Sorry, sir!

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.730
You two...

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:58.970
will be playing doubles together.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:00.910
Huh?

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:05.710
What?!

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.280
<b><i>Salaryman's Club</i></b>

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:40.090
What do you mean, we'll be playing doubles?!

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:43.240
<b><i>#08: Breakthrough</i></b>

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:43.680
My brother plays singles, 
and I've got Ko-san—

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.100
Wait...

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:50.480
Takeda's retiring from play
 and becoming a coach.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:53.990
It's not a bad thing.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:58.940
I'd been considering it for 
a while. You knew that, Toya.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:03.030
But you overcame your 
performance anxiety recently.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:04.340
That's why I'm doing this.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:05.160
Huh?

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:08.320
In our match against Unisics 
at the corporate tournament,

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.870
I played at full strength and lost.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:16.340
I gave everything I had as 
a player and still lost.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.350
Now that Usuyama-san's joined the team,

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:24.690
when I thought about what I could
 do to help SunBev improve,

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.670
I realized I had to become a coach.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:27.680
But...

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:31.890
I'm engaging with badminton 
on the path of my choosing.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.190
Ko-san...

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:36.630
Takeda's always paying close 
attention to his surroundings.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.570
He'll make a good coach.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:43.280
I hope you'll provide us with some
 good guidance, Coach Takeda.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.590
You can count on me, team!

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:48.980
Try not to let my coaching 
throw you off the team.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:51.160
See? It went straight to his head.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:04:00.490
Now then, our goal is winning the S/J League.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:04.390
It won't be like the number two league 
we were playing in until last year.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:07.290
We'll be going hard with a winning lineup!

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:07.970
Yes, sir!

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:10.440
Doubles 1 will be Tatsu and Shiratori.

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:13.200
We'll start with you two 
locking down a win for us.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:13.940
Yes, sir.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:15.860
Usuyama, you'll be playing singles.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:18.370
Make up for the gap in your 
badminton career with grit.

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:19.150
Yes, sir!

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.510
Doubles 2 will be Sota and Toya.

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:24.440
You've got the potential for dramatic change.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:25.990
I've got high hopes for you.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.060
Yes, sir!

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:28.900
Yes, sir.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.630
Hey, you're picking out 
your bell peppers again.

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:37.220
I'll eat them later.

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:38.670
Yeah, right.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:44.090
Are you really okay with Ko-san's decision?

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:53.020
I think some part of me blamed 
Ko-san for our losses.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:05:00.940
Even though I made a ton of 
mistakes, he'd always apologize.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:03.150
I took advantage of that.

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:08.320
I don't think Ko-san will regret 
choosing to become a coach.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:12.410
So I want to give 100% to 
everything I can do, too.

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:17.120
I mean, it does feel a little weird 
having you as my partner.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.220
But...

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:19.810
Bro?

00:05:20.390 --> 00:05:21.840
I'm going for a run.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.190
Huh? Hey, Bro!

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:32.600
Usuyama, you'll be playing singles.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.270
You two will be playing doubles together.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.680
It's kinda quiet today.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:52.650
Is Takeda late to his first day as a coa—

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:54.700
Hey, ow, ow, ow!

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:59.040
My brother's not here yet, either.

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:01.380
B-Bad news, guys!

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:03.800
Office gossip again?

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:04.760
It's Sota!

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:07.840
He... He submitted his team resignation!

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:16.140
Saeki, don't you need to go to practice?

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:17.980
Oh, you know...

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:21.750
You dumb piece of shit!

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:22.670
What the?

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:24.440
You didn't tell me you were quitting!

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.330
What do you think you're doing?!

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:27.690
You're always—

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:30.130
We're in the office.

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:33.160
Sorry about the noise.

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:38.290
So what's this about you quitting 
when we're just getting started?

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:41.400
I'm just a filler player now.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:44.190
I might as well not be on the team.

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:45.600
Why would you say that?

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:51.260
It was already over once 
I was taken off singles.

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.560
I was swapped to doubles 
because I was left over

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:58.230
after Usuyama-san joined 
the team and Ko-san quit.

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:00.390
Nobody thinks that.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:07.110
I wouldn't be so sure. Deep down, 
you feel sorry for me, didn't you?

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:08.550
What?

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:13.730
Having you play doubles with me out 
of pity just makes me feel miserable.

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:15.200
I want to play with—

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:16.950
Spare me that crap.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:18.620
Honestly, it's annoying.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:26.180
I see.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:42.550
Hey, good evening.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:51.940
