00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:38.580
13.

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:38.580
They all said no.

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:42.880
Are you giving up?

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:44.640
Bro...

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:48.090
What do you want? I've still 
got time until the deadline.

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:50.890
You're always like this.

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:55.730
You believe everything's possible 
and keep trying until the end.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:58.310
I think that's an amazing quality.

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:08.740
Wait!

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:13.120
Help me out, Bro.

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:17.530
I can't get anyone to do it, 
not on this schedule.

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:20.240
Ten o'clock, huh?

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:22.170
We might just make it.

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:23.250
Huh?!

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:28.170
What? You're playing games 
now? Is this a joke?

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:32.350
Ugh, I'm screwed.

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:33.680
Gotcha.

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:36.070
What? A rare monster?

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:39.850
Send the documents to 
this address right away.

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:43.800
He's a designer living in 
America who I play games with.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:45.230
I'm pretty sure he's good.

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:49.490
All right.

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:51.380
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:52.450
Yes.

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:55.540
Thanks for accepting this rush job.

00:14:55.540 --> 00:15:01.250
I figured Sota must be in serious trouble, 
since he sounded so desperate.

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:03.910
<i>Don't worry, I'll make it work.</i>

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:06.310
Thank you very much!

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:25.340
Design Ver_02

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:25.340
Design Ver_01

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:26.710
Design Ver_02

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:26.710
Design Ver_02

00:15:37.470 --> 00:15:40.970
Sir, have you gotten a chance to look 
at the rough draft of the design?

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:42.500
<i>It's fantastic!</i>

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:46.010
<i>How'd you get such a big-name 
designer to do the job?</i>

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:50.040
My brother's an amazing guy.

00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:53.700
I'll come back to the office 
after running home real quick.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:00.100
I'm exhausted.

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:03.900
What the hell's all this?!

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:05.650
Our home.

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:08.670
How does this happen in only three days?!

00:16:09.020 --> 00:16:10.610
Unbelievable.

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:17.660
I'll play doubles.

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:19.120
Huh?

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:26.330
I feel like Villager A might actually 
have some value when I'm with you.

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:29.350
What does that even mean? I don't get it.

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:33.220
But I was reminded of something today.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:35.740
You really are amazing.

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:39.030
You're amazing, Bro!

00:16:41.940 --> 00:16:45.170
Co-op might not be so bad after all.

00:16:51.850 --> 00:16:54.020
Hey, Shiratori-kun.

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:54.990
What is it?

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:58.200
Is it true Miyazumi-san's 
getting married soon?

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:01.480
What is that, an urban legend?

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:04.300
Takeda-san made that up, didn't he?

00:17:04.300 --> 00:17:08.170
I heard some secretaries gossiping about it.

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:13.380
They said Miyazumi-san might accept 
the promotion he'd been turning down.

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:17.600
So he's settling down and getting married...

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:19.350
And quitting badminton, too.

00:17:19.570 --> 00:17:20.230
Huh?

00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:24.060
Wasn't he turning down the promotion 
so he could play badminton?

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:26.230
He's quitting?

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:29.980
<b>Saitama Matsugishi Public 
Elementary School Song</b>

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:36.650
Does Tatsu-san seem kind 
of weird to you today?

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:37.860
<i>This is our chance!</i>

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:46.500
Restaurant Isuzu

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:47.110
I don't believe this.

00:17:47.110 --> 00:17:50.920
Why didn't the old man go for the jump smash?

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:53.190
You're unusually agitated.

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:55.130
Here are your Fukaya green onions.

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:57.070
Is he even trying?!

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:01.220
He used to complain about 
him jumping too much.

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:05.180
I do feel like he's started making
 more defensive plays, though.

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:08.050
They say love changes people.

00:18:08.050 --> 00:18:10.340
Yeah, that's the rumor going around.

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:12.520
Is it true that he's getting married soon?

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:14.880
I refuse to believe it!

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:19.240
There's no way that crude 
old man has a girlfriend!

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:22.140
You two are turning into a great pair.

00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:23.580
I'm pissed, okay?!

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:28.670
I'll smash his stupid, grinning face!

00:18:39.730 --> 00:18:41.120
Executive Director Oshitari!

00:18:41.440 --> 00:18:44.140
You boys seem to be having a good time.

00:18:44.380 --> 00:18:46.600
Mikoto, apologize! Quick!

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:49.100
Executive director?

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:53.230
It's an alien from Planet Green Onion!

00:18:54.790 --> 00:18:57.900
Hey, don't laugh. It's rude...

00:19:06.100 --> 00:19:12.140
The badminton team failed to put up a 
decent showing at the recent tournament.

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:15.420
Can you afford to be lazing around here?

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:17.570
We made it all the way to the sixth round.

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:21.630
Meaning you're a weak team that didn't 
make it onto the winner's podium.

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:27.820
I believe your captain is 
Miyazumi-kun from Sales, right?

00:19:27.820 --> 00:19:32.690
It's irresponsible of him not to keep 
someone so rude on a shorter leash.

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:34.650
It's not that big a deal.

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:40.700
I've had doubts about Miyazumi-kun's 
actions for some time now.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:42.730
He does whatever he wants,

00:19:42.730 --> 00:19:45.060
like using other companies' 
distribution systems

00:19:45.060 --> 00:19:46.820
and poaching talented 
employees for his team.

00:19:46.820 --> 00:19:48.880
I bet the rest of Sales gets
 left to clean up his mess

00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:52.040
because he devotes all his 
attention to badminton.

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:56.090
That's not true! He gives 120% to both!

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:58.130
What's gotten into you?

00:19:58.130 --> 00:19:59.810
Mikoto, enough already.

00:19:59.810 --> 00:20:01.400
We're really sorry.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:06.520
Everyone in the sales department 
supports the badminton team.

00:20:06.520 --> 00:20:09.970
It motivates us to meet their expectations!

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:13.860
And besides, we'll win 
the S/J League this year!

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:18.760
Win? Now <i>that's</i> a funny joke.

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:23.660
A Badaryman doesn't go back on his word.

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:28.690
You wouldn't know since you're always 
sitting up there on your corporate throne,

00:20:29.010 --> 00:20:30.870
but this team is strong.

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:32.690
We won't lose.

00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:16.350
Good morning.

00:22:16.350 --> 00:22:19.310
Good morning. Hung over again?

00:22:20.860 --> 00:22:23.970
Huh? Did he head straight 
to see a client today?

00:22:23.970 --> 00:22:26.990
Miyazumi-san's on a business 
trip to Osaka starting today.

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:28.420
Didn't anyone tell you?

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:29.970
<b>Sakaki</b>

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:29.970
<b>Amano</b>

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:29.970
<b>Miyazumi</b>

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:29.970
<b>Business Trip</b>

00:22:36.020 --> 00:22:37.080
Miyazumi-san!

00:22:39.030 --> 00:22:41.290
What's the matter?

00:22:43.600 --> 00:22:45.850
You've been acting weird recently.

00:22:45.850 --> 00:22:50.250
You didn't even mention your business trip, 
and you've been slacking off at practice.

00:22:50.940 --> 00:22:53.470
Didn't we say we'd win the S/J League?

00:22:55.520 --> 00:23:00.350
I was going to tell you once 
I got back, but whatever.

00:23:00.570 --> 00:23:01.450
What?

00:23:02.830 --> 00:23:06.480
I'd like to dissolve our doubles team.
